      en: "Višegrad is one of the most famous historical cities in eastern Bosnia, extending impressively along the banks of the Drina River and fully surrounded by dramatic and steep rocky gorges. The absolute main attraction of the city, which has brought it worldwide recognition, is the monumental Ottoman Mehmed Paša Sokolović Bridge, an architectural masterpiece from the 16th century that has been officially declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site. This iconic bridge provided the central inspiration for the famous novel \"The Bridge on the Drina\" by Nobel Prize laureate Ivo Andrić. More recently, acclaimed film director Emir Kusturica built Andrićgrad (Stone Town), a massive cultural and arts center in the heart of Višegrad that evokes the various historical epochs of the Balkans and currently stands as one of the region's largest tourist attractions."
