      en: "Lopare is a charming municipality in the northeast of Bosnia and Herzegovina, nestled in the gentle, green foothills of the Majevica Mountains. The region is known nationwide for its fertile soils and mild microclimate, which create ideal conditions for fruit growing, particularly for the cultivation of high-quality plums. In addition to thriving agriculture, traditional wood processing and ecotourism are playing an increasingly important role, as the pristine hilly landscapes attract many nature lovers and hikers to the area."
